1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,680
Branch operations and incident recovery for fast-food and takeaway chains.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:19,680
Switch branches to see what each store can sell with its own stock and equipment.

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:24,480
Akasaka tracks its own ingredients and stock balances.

4
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,960
Record a stock receipt in the ingredient's measurement unit.

5
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:37,960
Save the receipt with a reason. The balance and movement history update.

6
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:47,960
Choose which shared ingredients this branch tracks. Linking alone does not add stock.

7
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:55,960
Branch inventory keeps quantities, reservations and recorded movements together.

8
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:01,960
Ingredient definitions are shared across the chain. Stock quantities stay local.

9
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:12,160
Akasaka's rice cooker is a branch-owned asset. Report a problem directly from its card.

10
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:26,440
Confirm the cooker fault: nine veggie bowls need support within 60 minutes.

11
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:35,440
No source is eligible yet. Support needs an approved route to the receiving branch.

12
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:46,720
Request AI advice for manager review. No operational changes happen automatically.

13
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:53,000
Approve the demo route from Shinjuku East to Akasaka: 10 minutes of travel.

14
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,680
Eligible: 9 bowls · 18 minutes · ¥0

15
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:59,680
Review source, destination and quantity. Sending does not reserve stock.

16
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:04,360
The source approves the request and reserves ingredients.

17
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:07,640
Starting preparation consumes ingredients at the source branch.

18
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:11,040
Confirm dispatch of the prepared dishes in this demo.

19
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:15,320
The receiving branch confirms the prepared meals have arrived in this demo.

20
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:19,600
Nine bowls marked Received. Equipment repair and incident resolution remain separate.
